  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Light of wavelength <math><msub><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></math> falls on a cathode plate inside a vacuum tube as shown in the figure. The work function of the cathode surface is <math><mi>ϕ</mi></math> and the anode is a wire mesh of conducting material kept at a distance d from the cathode. A potential difference V is maintained between the electrodes. If the minimum de Broglie wavelength of the electrons passing through the anode is <math><msub><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></math> which of the following statement(s) is(are) true ?<br ><br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/Phy_Papr2_10..jpg\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "kbIAE",
      "text": "For large potential difference <math> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>V</mtext> <mo>≫</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mi>ϕ</mi> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>e</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>,</mo> <msub> <mi>&lambda;</mi> <mtext>e</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </math> is approximately halved if V is made four times",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "j5998",
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>&lambda;</mi> <mtext>e</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </math> increases at the same rate as <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>&lambda;</mi> <mtext>ph</mtext> </msub> <mo>for</mo> <msub> <mi>&lambda;</mi> <mtext>ph</mtext> </msub> <mo>&lt;</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>hc</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mi>ϕ</mi> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "TtIrv",
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>&lambda;</mi> <mo>ⅇ</mo> </msub> </mrow> </math> is approximately halved, if d is doubled",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "xaDg7",
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>&lambda;</mi> <mo>ⅇ</mo> </msub> </mrow> </math> decreases with increase in <math> <mrow> <mi>ϕ</mi> <mo>and</mo> <msub> <mi>&lambda;</mi> <mtext>ph</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&lambda;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></math><br />Kinetic energy of <math><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> reaching the anode will be<br /><math><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&lambda;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi></math><br />Now <math><msub><mrow><mi>&lambda;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&lambda;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math><br />If <math><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>≫</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></math><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>&lambda;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&lambda;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math><br />If <math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></math><br /><math><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&lambda;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≃</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&lambda;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
    "image": null
  },
